  "question": {
    "text": "In the chemical reaction $A \\rightarrow B$, what is the order of the reaction? Given that, the rate of reaction doubles if the concentration of $A$ is increased four times.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "zFUt1",
      "text": "$2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "qajMv",
      "text": "$1.5$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "mzJMX",
      "text": "$0.5$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "27t2v",
      "text": "$1$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "We know, $r_1=k[A]^{\\mathrm{n}}$    ....(i)\nIf conc. of $A$ is increased four times rate of reaction on doubles.\n$2 r_1=k[4 A]^{\\mathrm{n}}$     ....(ii) \nDivide Eq. (ii) by (i).\n$\\frac{2 r_i}{r_1}=\\frac{k(4 A)^n}{k(A)^n}$\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad 2=(4)^{\\mathrm{n}} \\Rightarrow 2 \\mathrm{n}=(2)^{2 \\mathrm{n}} \\Rightarrow n=0.5$",
    "image": null
  },
